================================================================================
CHALLENGE: THE NETWORK IP SWEEPER (Host Discovery)
================================================================================
SCENARIO: You are on a network (192.168.1.x) and need to find all active
devices. Checking each one manually takes too long.

1. CLASS: 'HostCheckTask' (implements Callable<String>)
   - Constructor: Takes 'String ip'.
   - 'call()' logic:
        * Use 'InetAddress.getByName(ip).isReachable(500)'.
        * If true, return ip + " is UP".
        * If false, return null.

2. MAIN:
   - Use 'ExecutorService executor = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(20);'
   - Loop from i = 1 to 254.
   - String targetIp = "192.168.1." + i;
   - Submit tasks and collect results.

EXPECTATION: The scanner should sweep the entire subnet in seconds.
Only the "UP" hosts should be printed to the console.
================================================================================